index 7ae6f77..893f797 100644
--- a/docs/modules/compiler/spec.md
+++ b/docs/modules/compiler/spec.md
@@ -90,6 +90,14 @@ object rebuilds both MC objects. The 64 KiB bound controls reuse only and does
 not limit compiled function size. This lifecycle does not change code publication,
 relocation, trap checks or guest execution semantics.

+FastRA register-class metadata may persist in the worker's CompileContext.
+Every function still freezes its reserved-register set and runs
+`CgRegisterClassInfo::runOnCgFunction`, preserving invalidation for target,
+callee-saved registers, reservation masks and allocation-order policy. Clear
+function and workaround pointers when allocation ends, including exception exits;
+retain only target-derived tables. Context copies start with independent caches.
+Register choice and definition operand order must match a fresh class-info object.
+
 ### LazyJIT stub publish monotonicity

 In multithread LazyJIT, each function stub's `jmp` target is published monotonically:
